    "field": "Aerosol-cloud interactions",
    "problem": "The largest source of uncertainty in climate prediction is the difficulty of characterizing clouds, as models inadequately represent how small-scale interactions between aerosol particles and water droplets affect large-scale cloud properties like brightness, lifetime, and precipitation.",
    "method": "The paper proposes an integrated approach combining new observational programmes, numerical models, laboratory investigations, and field studies, tightly linked with monitoring networks, to quantify the effects of anthropogenic aerosols on large-scale cloud properties.",
    "task": "The task is to improve the understanding of small-scale cloud processes, particularly aerosol-cloud interactions, to reduce the significant uncertainty that clouds contribute to climate prediction models and to clarify their role in the climate system.",
